    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. i see both sides but it feels a bit vague. for the \"against\" part, is it just about the cost for companies, or are there deeper issues with sovereignty? like, if a country wants to change its own laws to suit its specific economy, would this treaty basically stop them from doing that? i'm trying to understand if this is just a business cost thing or a bigger loss of control for individual nations.",
