      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Proponents of the treaty argue that in the face of transboundary crises like climate change, national self-interest must yield to collective global necessity. They suggest that the current paradigm of absolute sovereignty is insufficient when ecological damage impacts every nation regardless of where it originates. Therefore, the \"moral ground\" rests on the idea that international cooperation and agreed-upon shared standards are essential for planetary survival.",
      "source": "target",
